ry that. \n\nSo, the next tool call would be get_metrics with a query like "up{job=\'user-service\'}" to check if user-service is up. If it\'s down, that\'s a fault. Then repeat for other services. \n\nBut since the user might have multiple services, maybe check all in one go. However, the get_metrics tool can only take one query at a time. \n\nSo, first, check user-service. Then post-service, and so on. \n\nAlternatively, check the overall health of the cluster. \n\nBut the user\'s main goal is to find the root cause of any faults. So, the first step is to identify which services are not functioning correctly. \n\nTherefore, the next tool call should be get_metrics with a query to check the up status of each service. Let\'s start with user-service.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"query": "up{job=\\"user-service\\"}"}', 'name': 'get_metrics'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-86807e8e917236ea', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1125, 'prompt_tokens': 2463, 'total_tokens': 3588, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe22-0880-7213-959f-96a5595da081-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_metrics', 'args': {'query': 'up{job="user-service"}'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-86807e8e917236ea', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2463, 'output_tokens': 1125, 'total_tokens': 3588}), ToolMessage(content='("{\'resultType\': \'vector\', \'result\': []}", 12)', id='41c743e4-f1d0-4971-88cd-0022307ab2af', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-86807e8e917236ea'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='419bdc34-fa25-40fb-851e-41e5c